fact WorkItem(id: "WI-064", description: some(value: "Add fold / reduce / map / filter combinators to stdlib. Currently anthill.prelude.Iteration only has split; Collection has insert + empty. No higher-order combinators. Blocks ergonomic list processing — every user program that wants to sum a list has to hand-roll recursion. Add: fold_left(xs, init, f), fold_right(xs, init, f), map(xs, f), filter(xs, pred), for_each(xs, f) in anthill.prelude.Iteration (polymorphic over Iterator[T]). Definitions via rules over Iteration.split. Acceptance: a reduce-the-list-to-sum integration test passes end-to-end."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-275"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-06T19:42:56Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-064", author: "user", content: "REFRESH NEEDED + re-rooted 2026-06-06: this is the combinator layer under WI-409 (the real driver — map/find/fold used in cli/parse.anthill ParseArgs instead of recursion). (1) The original 'definitions via rules over Iteration.split' approach is superseded by the WI-380 substrate — Stream ops (splitFirst/collect/takeN) are now OPERATIONS with default bodies over splitFirst[Elem,Eff], so map/fold/filter/find should follow that style (explicit [Elem,Eff] element threading, DELIVERED), on Stream/Iterable, not 'rules over split'. (2) Now depends_on WI-275 — the combinators take a Function param and apply it (HOF), which is the proven blocker (probe: applying a function-typed param / lambda arg does not type-check). (3) The element-type CHANGE map needs (Stream[T=A]->Stream[T=B]) is the explicit-type-param style WI-380/393 delivered; the projection/path-dependent cluster (WI-376/397...) is NOT required.", at: "2026-06-06T16:02:48Z")

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-064", name: "first-real-map")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-064", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED 2026-06-06 (990c4d0): fold_left/fold_right/find (eager, on Stream over splitFirst, alongside collect/takeN) + map (lazy MappedStream carrier providing Stream) in stdlib. All work typecheck+EVAL (eval_test::wi064_stdlib_combinators_fold_map_find: reduce-to-sum=10 acceptance; direction-sensitive folds via subtraction -6 vs 2; map collect 234 / map+fold 9 / empty 0; find first/head/none). Usable with NAMED transform/predicate ops (WI-275 eta); a List is the receiver via List-provides-Stream. Fn params carry E=Eff (effectful-transform soundness, /code-review). DEFERRED, all tracked: (1) FILTER -> WI-410 (blocked WI-356: a kept element returned verbatim needs the source head's element type threaded through splitFirst's Pair destructure; off WI-409 critical path); (2) map's recursive splitFirst self-dispatched to MappedStream.splitFirst when UNqualified -> latent typer bug WI-411, worked around with qualified Stream.splitFirst(src) (the user's original fragment was typecheck-only, never eval'd, so this was newly surfaced — VERIFY EVAL, not just typecheck); (3) map needs explicit [Dst,Eff] (output element/effect not inferred from transform/source — WI-275-class refinement; user accepted explicit-args interim). WI-409 (map+find+fold in ParseArgs) is now UNBLOCKED.", at: "2026-06-06T19:42:56Z")
